{"skill":{"slug":"word-reader","displayName":"Word Reader"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770700102926,"changelog":"支持 .docx 和 .doc 格式的 Word 文档读取，提取文本、表格、元数据等","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"DEVELOPMENT.md","size":4758,"sha256":"4c54685ab51623fc875f6157589ae65d58ea212f1eef935e39dc65a22acfe9be","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"PUBLISHING.md","size":3702,"sha256":"8f50a1732b00bd4210fe70891d8e6f2923d6daff86301550abbcce742f00a471","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":4080,"sha256":"bc703a20f1eb2921d00865b19b24c195963cff2e87885c88958f42871b5b4ee8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4949,"sha256":"dd40f6e88308a5c87c2f1c1074110c0b6ca8982b37d92340d474fe0f63ba8f8f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"demo.sh","size":2290,"sha256":"f396e27ea2ef31ef3503e20b8f554546fedc8e0bfeb2db1856725db226c64acb","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"install.sh","size":2725,"sha256":"ea7ad0675aa3988ca3403fc16270694870e14b1335fd928b91ad5d9d74db0ff2","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/read_word.py","size":14474,"sha256":"877aeed6a2faac289a358dd9f35f715e989d3d093807a6ab41f44f54945ab7ea","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill.json","size":1391,"sha256":"eef8303929f53b2a1edadf43ea6f52612a63179a04301fc8b8a52f645fa23d2b","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"test.md","size":1126,"sha256":"8b9797feee1ebec1e686619df1d52aba343aeaefa349760fe439cd038c971be9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2024,"sha256":"f781ad94ea19282b89fdcfce603b618bdfadff481f864c5451d462055b019f52","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789057549879,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e93d0ff3bbc641e688a689395b335c43d82a7c7f4a1492d74b7ecb0bf7baeedd","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e93d0ff3bbc641e688a689395b335c43d82a7c7f4a1492d74b7ecb0bf7baeedd","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: word-reader\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its installation process involving privileged commands and potentially risky Python package management. Specifically, the `SKILL.md` file explicitly instructs the agent to execute `sudo apt-get install antiword -y` for `.doc` file support, and the `install.sh` script also uses `sudo` for installing `pip` via system package managers (`apt`, `yum`) and `pip install python-docx --break-system-packages`. While these actions are for legitimate dependency installation, the use of `sudo` grants elevated privileges, and `--break-system-packages` can modify system-managed Python environments, representing risky capabilities without clear malicious intent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162679674},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":33,"checkedAt":1789057549879},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill appears to read Word documents as advertised, but its installer can make system-level package changes and its outputs may save sensitive document contents without strong warnings.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using system package managers and modifying the system-managed Python environment is broader than needed for a document reader, where a virtual environment or explicit manual dependency setup would be more contained.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The recommended installer and metadata include unpinned python-docx installation, use of --break-system-packages, chmod changes, and sudo package-manager commands for pip or antiword without clear warnings about system impact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are focused on parsing user-specified Word files and directories; no hidden prompt override, persistence instruction, exfiltration, or unrelated network behavior was found.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No services, cron jobs, startup hooks, or cross-session backdoors were found; persistence is limited to dependency installation, executable permission changes, and user-selected output files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The document-reading, metadata extraction, batch processing, and optional output-file writing are coherent with a Word extraction skill and are mostly disclosed in the usage docs.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review the installer before running it. Prefer installing dependencies in a virtual environment, avoid --break-system-packages, and only use sudo or antiword if you specifically need legacy .doc support. Treat extracted text, metadata, and batch output files as potentially sensitive, especially when processing business or personal documents.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: Extraction of full document text and metadata, including batch output to disk, is expected for this skill, but the artifacts under-warn users that Word files and saved results may contain sensitive content.\n[LP3] unexpected: The concern is partially supported: the skill does not define narrow permission boundaries, though the actual instructions remain focused on user-specified document paths rather than broad autonomous access.\n[PE2] expected: sudo appears for dependency setup, especially optional .doc support and pip installation fallback; this is purpose-related but high-impact and not sufficiently cautioned.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only user-facing text is a localization/usability issue, not a security concern by itself.\n[SDI-1] expected: Writing output files and setting executable permissions are disclosed workflow/setup behaviors, but output writes may overwrite user-selected paths and store sensitive extracted content.\n[SDI-2] expected: Calling antiword for legacy .doc parsing is expected for .doc support, but it expands parser attack surface for untrusted documents.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess calls use explicit argument lists with shell=False, so command injection evidence is weak; the remaining risk is reliance on an external parser.\n[T08] unexpected: The static finding is supported: install.sh installs unpinned python-docx and prefers --break-system-packages, creating supply-chain and environment-integrity risk rather than evidence of a malicious dependency.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789057549879}}}}}